namespace pdg {
/**
\class Part
\ingroup Animation
\brief An independently animated part owned by a Sprite.

Create a Part by calling \ref Sprite::createPart "createPart()" on a Sprite
instance. Part cannot be constructed directly with \c new.

\code{.js}
const sprite = new pdg.Sprite();
const part = sprite.createPart("hand");
part.moveTo(new pdg.Point(12, 0), 0.25, pdg.easeInOutQuad);
\endcode

Part inherits Animated's programmed movement, rotation and size operations.
All animation durations are floating-point seconds. The owning Sprite advances
its attached Parts; do not also call animate() on an attached Part every frame.

Bone binding is optional. getBoneId() is safe on an unbound Part and returns
\c pdg.boneId_None. Binding and hierarchy belong to Part, not Animated.
Part has an optional PhysicsBody through its physics property.
setupPhysicsBody() creates it explicitly; otherwise physics returns pdg.PhysicsBody.NoPhysics.
Only setupPhysicsBody()/removePhysicsBody() can change the property association.
Compare physics with pdg.PhysicsBody.NoPhysics to test absence.
Removing a Part detaches its body and stops automatic stepping.

A retained Part remains valid after removal from its Sprite; isAttached()
reports false and its independent local transform remains available.
*/
}
